// Digits are accumulated eight at a time into a machine integer, and each
// full chunk is folded into the running value with one multiply-and-add:
// value = value * 10^8 + chunk. That is one BigInt operation per eight
// characters instead of one per character, which is the whole reason for the
// chunked representation. Underscores are accepted as digit separators inside
// the digit run even though the language's own lexer rejects them.

